  "extraction_notes": [
    "Public PDF SHA-256 verified as d86c380303f357639bf9f38791dcda5b6360e70377cd3309c98b16126f9cf97e.",
    "The datasheet static electrical-characteristics heading specifies TJ = 25 degC unless otherwise specified; all static-table values above preserve that bias.",
    "The public PDF does not state a document revision identifier.",
    "RDS(on) typical values are 2.6 mOhm at VGS = 10 V and ID = 15 A, and 3.2 mOhm at VGS = 4.5 V and ID = 12 A. The corresponding published maximum values are 3.3 mOhm and 4.0 mOhm, respectively, on p. 2.",
    "VGS(th) has MIN = 1.0 V and MAX = 2.5 V at VDS = VGS and ID = 250 uA; the TYP column is blank.",
    "BVDSS is a minimum 30 V at VGS = 0 V and ID = 250 uA. The breakdown-voltage temperature coefficient is typical 19 mV/degC referenced to 25 degC at ID = 1 mA.",
    "IDSS is maximum 1.0 uA at VDS = 24 V and VGS = 0 V, and maximum 150 uA at the same bias with TJ = 125 degC.",
    "Ciss, Coss, and Crss are typical values at VGS = 0 V, VDS = 15 V, f = 1.0 MHz. The capacitance figure is also digitized as separate Ciss, Coss, and Crss traces.",
    "Qg is typical 34 nC and maximum 50 nC at VDS = 15 V, VGS = 4.5 V, and ID = 12 A. Qgd is typical 12 nC, Qgs1 is typical 9.1 nC, Qgs2 is typical 2.5 nC, Qoss is typical 21 nC, and Qrr is typical 36 nC and maximum 54 nC.",
    "Body-diode VSD is maximum 1.0 V at TJ = 25 degC, IS = 12 A, VGS = 0 V. trr is typical 39 ns and maximum 59 ns at TJ = 25 degC, IF = 12 A, VDD = 15 V, and di/dt = 100 A/us.",
    "Thermal resistance is maximum RthetaJC = 1.05 K/W, maximum RthetaJA = 50 K/W for PCB mount, and maximum RthetaJA = 110 K/W for junction-to-ambient, p. 1.",
    "The plotted points are manual digitizations of the visible traces in p. 3 Fig. 1 and Fig. 3, p. 4 Fig. 5 and Fig. 7. Logarithmic axes and the stated pulse-width, voltage, current, frequency, and temperature conditions are preserved.",
    "Absolute maximum ratings include VDS = 30 V, VGS = +/-20 V, ID = 161 A at TC = 25 degC and VGS = 10 V, IDM = 620 A, PD = 140 W at TC = 25 degC, and TJ = -55 to +175 degC."
  ],
